                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cf1921df-35ce-37ff-8857-27ac03d50bae",
                        "entry_id": "874dc63b-f784-3228-adb0-99c271b07b20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To mumble, speak unclearly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "ambitransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4d792af-b66c-4224-aff0-3e3a35652411",
                                "sense_id": "cf1921df-35ce-37ff-8857-27ac03d50bae",
                                "text": "Who mump their passion, and who, grimly smiling,\nStill thus address the fair with voice beguiling […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4843a173-d015-322e-a3df-f9cf17d9a367",
                        "entry_id": "874dc63b-f784-3228-adb0-99c271b07b20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To move the lips with the mouth closed; to mumble, as in sulkiness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e312dc1-38ac-4bc1-8be2-25dadce7c65d",
                                "sense_id": "4843a173-d015-322e-a3df-f9cf17d9a367",
                                "text": "He mumps, and lowres, and hangs the lip […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9da9c7bd-2704-339d-90fb-e737845cf5ec",
                        "entry_id": "874dc63b-f784-3228-adb0-99c271b07b20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To beg, especially if using a repeated phrase."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b2f4a479-0679-30af-b4d7-6c08b68bac3f",
                        "entry_id": "874dc63b-f784-3228-adb0-99c271b07b20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To deprive of (something) by cheating; to impose upon."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fb49eac5-fa97-3f53-9002-f78b3fa7050f",
                        "entry_id": "874dc63b-f784-3228-adb0-99c271b07b20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To cheat; to deceive; to play the beggar."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "06c3d92d-3a29-459c-99e3-d171b6989d14",
                                "sense_id": "fb49eac5-fa97-3f53-9002-f78b3fa7050f",
                                "text": "Your ministerial directors blustered like tragic tyrants here; and then went mumping with a sore leg in America, canting, and whining, and complaining of faction, which represented them as friends to a revenue from the colonies."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dcc856fb-6ffc-3a27-ae8d-5cdeceef7e61",
                        "entry_id": "874dc63b-f784-3228-adb0-99c271b07b20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To be sullen or sulky."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5555beb8-6c84-4e43-958e-115d09b7bf91",
                                "sense_id": "dcc856fb-6ffc-3a27-ae8d-5cdeceef7e61",
                                "text": "The Christian also spurns the pinched and mumping sick-room attitude, and the lives of saints are full of a kind of callousness to diseased conditions of body which probably no other human records show."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a05ed3e4-e249-4e8f-98e6-d97844da1320",
                                "sense_id": "dcc856fb-6ffc-3a27-ae8d-5cdeceef7e61",
                                "text": "It remained necessary to make a shift at bearing yourself like a man; not mumping, not moping."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
